{"title":"Mathematics competition","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Mathematics competitions</b> are contests that typically challenge top <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics\" title=\"Mathematics\">mathematics</a> students to solve problems more difficult than those typically tested by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Standardized_test\" title=\"Standardized test\">standardized tests</a> or in the classroom.\n</p><p>Math competitions differ widely in difficulty and content.  Most test a broader range of mathematics curriculum and some focus on methods of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematical_problem_solving\" title=\"Mathematical problem solving\">mathematical problem solving</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions\" title=\"Resources for mathematics competitions\">Resources for mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Academic_competitions\" title=\"Academic competitions\">Academic competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=List_of_mathematics_competitions\" title=\"List of mathematics competitions\">List of mathematics competitions</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018033902\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.008 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.011 seconds\nPre